* ============================================================
* SET_CASE_NEAR_SHAKEDOWN_V1.DTS
*
* Purpose:
*   Focused shakedown for SETCASE / SET CASE and SETNEAR / SET NEAR.
*
* Scope:
*   - Direct SETCASE command
*   - Routed SET CASE command through cmd_set.cpp
*   - Direct SETNEAR command, if registered
*   - Routed SET NEAR command through cmd_set.cpp
*   - Basic SEEK behavior canary under SET NEAR OFF/ON
*
* Safety:
*   - Read-only
*   - No mutation
*   - No rebuild
* ============================================================

SET ECHO OFF
COLOR DEFAULT
ECHO ===== SET CASE / SET NEAR SHAKEDOWN V1 START =====

ECHO ===== PHASE 0 CLEAN START =====
SCHEMAS CLOSE
REL CLEAR ALL
SET FILTER TO
VERSION
STATUS

ECHO ===== PHASE 1 SETCASE DIRECT =====
SETCASE
SETCASE ON
SETCASE
SETCASE OFF
SETCASE

ECHO ===== PHASE 2 SET CASE THROUGH SET COMMAND =====
SET CASE
SET CASE ON
SET CASE
SET CASE OFF
SET CASE

ECHO ===== PHASE 3 SETNEAR DIRECT =====
ECHO [NOTE] If SETNEAR is not registered as a direct command yet, this section should show Unknown command.
SETNEAR
SETNEAR ON
SETNEAR
SETNEAR OFF
SETNEAR

ECHO ===== PHASE 4 SET NEAR THROUGH SET COMMAND =====
SET NEAR
SET NEAR ON
SET NEAR
SET NEAR OFF
SET NEAR

ECHO ===== PHASE 5 INVALID ARGUMENTS =====
SET CASE MAYBE
SET NEAR MAYBE

ECHO ===== PHASE 6 SEEK / NEAR CANARY SETUP =====
SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64
USE STUDENTS
SET INDEX TO STUDENTS
SET ORDER TO TAG LNAME
AREA
TOP
RECNO
SMARTLIST 5

ECHO ===== PHASE 7 SEEK WITH NEAR OFF =====
SET NEAR OFF
ECHO [EXPECT] SEEK WILX should be Not Found unless WILX exists exactly.
SEEK Wilx
RECNO
TUPLE *

ECHO ===== PHASE 8 SEEK WITH NEAR ON =====
SET NEAR ON
ECHO [CURRENT] If SEEK has not consumed SET NEAR yet, behavior may match NEAR OFF.
ECHO [FUTURE] Expected later: Near match, first key >= WILX.
SEEK Wilx
RECNO
TUPLE *

ECHO ===== PHASE 9 CLEAN SHUTDOWN =====
SET NEAR OFF
SET CASE OFF
SET ORDER TO 0
SET FILTER TO
CLOSE
SCHEMAS CLOSE
STATUS

ECHO ===== SET CASE / SET NEAR SHAKEDOWN V1 END =====
QUIT
